  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Ranipet?", answer: "Tell us your child's IB programme, subject, level and exam session, and we come back with tutors who genuinely teach that course. Since no school in the district runs the IB Diploma, the search happens nationally rather than by postcode, and the actual lesson time still gets fitted to your household afterward. Every match opens with a free trial, and a different tutor is offered if it does not feel right." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE tutors in Ranipet for Cambridge?", answer: "We do, delivered entirely online. Edify World School in Walajapet has started on the CAIE curriculum from Grade VI, but its oldest students have not reached Grade 10 yet, so most of the IGCSE demand reaching us from Ranipet actually belongs to families studying at a different school or boarding elsewhere. Matching runs off the precise code and tier, Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620 among the more common ones." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Ranipet?", answer: "They don't. Home visits from a tutor exist only in Gurugram and a few pockets of Delhi NCR. Everywhere else, Ranipet included, every lesson happens live over video, one to one, with a shared digital whiteboard standing in for a physical notebook. It is proper one-to-one teaching, just not delivered inside your house." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor in Ranipet cost?", answer: "Rate depends mainly on subject rarity, the level, how long each session runs, and how recently a tutor has taught that particular syllabus, confirmed in writing for your match before the trial happens. A Cambridge IGCSE Core subject typically costs less than an IB Diploma HL one, simply because more tutors can teach it well. Travel adds nothing to the number, and stopping or pausing never triggers a penalty." },
    { question: "Which schools in Ranipet offer IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Edify World School in Walajapet is the sole confirmed school in the district teaching toward a Cambridge qualification, and its cohort currently tops out at Grade VII, so a Grade 10 IGCSE batch does not exist there yet. Nothing in the district runs the IB Diploma, MYP or PYP; almost every other school here follows the Tamil Nadu State Board or CBSE." },
    { question: "My child boards at an IB school outside Ranipet. Can a tutor help during holidays?", answer: "Yes, and this is actually one of the more frequent enquiries we get from Ranipet, precisely because no school in the district teaches the Diploma or Middle Years Programme. The tutor gets matched to whatever syllabus, subject and level your child's boarding school follows, with sessions built around school holidays or an agreed evening slot during term if that school allows it." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial class before I commit?", answer: "Every match starts with one. Your child sits down online with the proposed tutor and works through material from their own syllabus, at no cost and with nothing signed beforehand. Once that lesson is done, the tutor writes up a short plan for the coming month, and only then do you decide whether to continue, adjust it, or ask for someone else." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments for a child in Ranipet?", answer: "Guidance only, never drafting. A tutor will help narrow down a workable research question, unpack what a specific assessment criterion is actually rewarding, sanity-check a data-collection plan, and mark up drafts honestly. Producing or substantially rewriting the assessed work itself falls outside IB's integrity rules, so that request gets turned down every time." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you help with for a Ranipet family?", answer: "Support runs across the subjects a boarding Ranipet student is most likely to be carrying: both Maths routes at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry and Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and History, plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay work." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students connected to Ranipet, not only the Diploma?", answer: "The full continuum is covered, not just the Diploma. For an MYP student that means criterion-level work across sciences and languages plus the Personal Project's process journal; for a PYP student it means reading mileage, writing practice, number confidence and the inquiry skills the Exhibition eventually calls on." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring as effective as in-person tuition for IB or IGCSE students in Ranipet?", answer: "Reasonably so, particularly given how few specialists for a specific HL subject or Cambridge code are based anywhere near Ranipet, and given that the district has no school running an active IGCSE exam cohort of its own yet. A shared digital whiteboard, screen-shared past papers and saved worked examples replace most of what sitting beside a student would offer, while opening up tutor choice nationally instead of locally." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors verified for Ranipet students?", answer: "Before ever being introduced to a family, a tutor's qualifications, recent experience with that exact subject and level, and understanding of how the relevant assessment criteria are actually applied all get checked. Because so few specialists for Ranipet's likely subject combinations exist locally, preference goes to people who have taught the current syllabus within the last year or two. The trial class is still where a family makes the final call." },
    { question: "When should my child in Ranipet start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Right when the course itself opens is ideal, Class 11 for the Diploma or Grade 9 for Cambridge IGCSE, since that leaves room to fix gaps before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades converge in the final year. Starting later still helps, provided sessions narrow in on the highest-value topics rather than trying to cover everything." },
    { question: "My child is switching from the Tamil Nadu State Board or CBSE to IGCSE in Ranipet. Can a tutor help?", answer: "Yes, and we see this often among households relocating through Ranipet's industrial estates. Content usually is not the problem; the way Cambridge phrases its questions is. Command words like explain, evaluate and justify need to be taught directly, ideally a term ahead of the actual switch, alongside real past-paper practice." },
    { question: "Can sessions happen on weekends or after school hours in Ranipet?", answer: "Yes. Weekday evenings and weekend mornings are what most families here book, planned around Golden Quadrilateral shift traffic, the worst of the summer heat, and the Pongal and Tamil New Year weeks. Slotting in a second session ahead of mocks or an exam series is not a problem." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not happy with the tutor in Ranipet?", answer: "Let us know and a replacement gets arranged. We check in with families roughly every few weeks precisely so a poor fit gets caught early rather than dragging on for a term, and since nothing here runs on a signed annual contract, stepping away costs nothing either." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with Edify World School, the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "No affiliation exists with Edify World School, any other school named here, the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge International or Pearson Edexcel. IB Gram runs independently; schools get mentioned only to show where Ranipet families are actually enrolled, and every tutor works to that school's calendar and the board's own published syllabus." },
  ],

